Z||000000||GAFIEROGT||02-13-2000||09:15 PM||||DOES ANYBODY HAVE ANY INFO ON WHAT 3.8 BUICK MOTORS WILL BOLT TO THE FIERO TRANSAXLE,AND WHAT FLYWHEEL TO USE WITH THE 5-SPEED,<BR>ALSO GEAR RATIOS ON THE FIVE SPEED.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||02-14-2000||07:35 AM||||The 3800 bolts up but you have to make a flywheel check <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.americancustomeng.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||02-14-2000||08:24 AM||||I know the 3800 will work with the Getrag/Muncie 5-speed if you have a new flywheel made.  But will the 3800 also bolt up to the Isuzu 5-speed in the same fashion?<P>I know conventional wisdom says the Isuzu can't handle the torque, but V8 Archie claims he has used engines with up to 300 hp with the Isuzu with no failures.  Plus the Isuzu gearboxes are plentiful and cheap, unlike the Getrag/Muncie.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||02-14-2000||09:11 AM||||What's the hp rating on the 3800 S/C?  Phil--don't you have the S/C?  What would the 3800 be like with an automatic?  I don't have the cash for a swap like that right now, but just curious.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||02-14-2000||09:49 AM||||People are going to start getting tired of my bragging about my 3800 but TOUGH. HP is 222(dyno tested)at the wheels, 270(est) at crank. The auto should be just about as peppy and stronger especially if you use the one from the donor car. Either way it will really leave a 2.8 in the weeds. 0-60 low 5s haven't done 1/4 mile yet but I understand that New England Dragway has a Pontiac show each year and you get unlimited runs for $5. Might just have to check it out. I've been driving for 40 yrs and have had various small/sports cars TR4, XKE, RX7, turbo Laser and none has been as much fun as the Fiero (although the Jag was close). ||||reg||1
